Security operations involve continuously protecting Azure environments against evolving threats. Instead of reacting only after an incident occurs, security teams monitor systems proactively and respond according to predefined procedures.

A typical security workflow includes:

* Continuous monitoring
* Threat detection
* Incident investigation
* Containment
* Remediation
* Recovery
* Post-incident analysis

# Real-Life Example:
For example, suspicious login activity may trigger an investigation that results in temporary account restrictions while administrators validate user identity.

# Real-Life Use Case:
A real-life use case is enterprise Security Operations Centers maintaining continuous visibility into cloud environments.

An effective security operations workflow strengthens organizational cyber resilience.
